[ceiling] These are the roofs of the two side-entry M5 square-nut pockets, at print Z13.2 above the Z9 pocket floors. The 4.2 mm pocket height accepts the stocked 4 mm nuts; screw preload bears on the 9 mm floor below each pocket. The retained roof is 1.8 mm thick, with the diameter-5.5 mm carrier screw passage through it. The native Tree(auto)/default slice has two bed-rooted bodies here: tree-1/interface-3 and tree-4/interface-4 in ready/tube-insertion-rigid-parts-h2c.support-audit.json, each with 12.24 mm build-up to its first interface and interface tops at Z12.68 beneath these Z13.2 roofs. The entries open at the two outer wing edges for support removal before the nuts are loaded or D is bolted to B. The audit records generated contacts and geometric removal access; physical removal effort and fixture load capacity remain unmeasured.
alternatives: Thickening the roofs downward reduces the 4.2 mm nut height clearance. Sloping the roofs changes the flat square-nut capture space. Opening these pockets through the mating face removes the roofs but adds a joint opening at the hard closure plane. The supported flat pockets retain the selected nut fit and the solid floor that receives preload.
