[ceiling] These are the two underside locating-key pocket roofs at print Z3.1. Their 8.2 by 6.2 mm rectangular openings admit B's 8 by 6 mm, 3 mm high keys with 0.1 mm clearance. The native Tree(auto)/default slice supplies bed-rooted tree-2/interface-1 and tree-3/interface-2, with 1.92 mm build-up to the first interfaces and interface tops at Z2.6 beneath the Z3.1 roofs. Both pockets open directly through D's underside for support removal before the carrier joint is assembled. These locating pockets register the metal-coupled joint; the two M5 screws secure it. The support audit establishes generated contacts and access, not physical removal effort.
alternatives: Removing the pockets prevents D from seating over the existing raised keys. Angling their roofs changes the rectangular key clearance and requires matching changes to B. Turning D over makes its liner and tube-contact geometry print down. The current orientation retains automatic support at the two accessible underside pockets.
