[thin] The 1.100 mm minima are the outer margins beside the two shallow rear-face witness grooves: Y48.9..50 and the negative twin. Each margin projects only 0.3 mm beyond the X38.2 groove floor over the upper 3 mm of the 15 mm half-jaw; the analytic STEP retains a complete 12 mm of stock below that footprint. At the lower jaw's nut pockets, the rear web from X35.15 to X38.2 remains 3.05 mm thick. The larger connected under-3 mm ranking also includes the 1.8 mm roofs above those side-entry pockets; the M5 nuts load their 9 mm floors below. The nominal diameter-30 mm pad-bearing disks end at Y47 or -47, leaving 1.1 mm to the grooves' inner edges. These are short witness margins and supported nut-capture roofs, rather than full-height 1.1 mm wing webs. This dimensional description supplies no as-printed strength or life rating.
alternatives: Removing the grooves and marking only with ink removes their narrow outer margins without enlarging the load-bearing disk, but requires renewing the marks after cleaning. Widening the wings increases the outer margin but adds stock beyond the nominal pad envelope. Increasing the nut roofs downward consumes the 0.2 mm total height clearance for the 4 mm nuts; retaining the 9 mm preload floor and accessible supported roof preserves the selected fastener fit.
